### SECTION 4: ANNOTATION (DERIVED - not raw output; hex -> dotted-IP decode) ###

Decoding rule for /proc/net/tcp: every IPv4 address is one little-endian 32-bit
word in hex (e.g. 020011AC -> AC.11.00.02 = 172.17.0.2), the port is big-endian
hex (e.g. A112 = 41234), and the 3rd field st is the socket state (01 = ESTABLISHED,
06 = TIME_WAIT, 0A = LISTEN).

S4.1 synthetic probe dial (section 2, connection held open 6s):
  container netns line:  020011AC:A9AA 010011AC:A112 01
    local  = 172.17.0.2:43434   (container eth0 address; non-loopback)
    remote = 172.17.0.1:41234   (docker0 gateway = host.docker.internal)
  host netns mirror of the same connection (section 1, host /proc/net/tcp):
    010011AC:A112 020011AC:A9AA 01  (local 172.17.0.1:41234 <- remote 172.17.0.2:43434)
  host ss mirror: ESTAB 172.17.0.1:41234 <- 172.17.0.2:43434 (python3 listener)
  Go-level net.Dial in the same container (section 3):
